---
/**
 * Privacy page — static policy, code-managed copy (edit here, not in CMS).
 * ⚠️ Contact details are placeholders; keep in sync with contact.astro and
 * Footer.astro.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/pages/PageHero.astro';

// Single source of the "last updated" date; hardcode, do not use the build date.
const lastUpdated = '2026-11-12';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Kadali"
  description="Kadali's privacy policy in plain words: no analytics, no tracking pixels, no cookies from this site, Cloudflare edge logs only, photos with consent."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="Privacy policy"
    kn="ಗೋಪ್ಯತೆ"
    lede="The whole policy without the usual fog: nothing collected, nothing tracked, nothing sold — because there is nothing to sell."
    tone="cream"
  />

  <article
    class="prose-kadali mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6"
  >
    <p class="font-ui text-sm text-stone">
      Last updated <time datetime={lastUpdated}>12 November 2026</time>.
    </p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No analytics, no tracking pixels, no advertising — there is none on this site.</li>
      <li>This site sets no cookies of its own.</li>
      <li>A WhatsApp or email message goes to the club, not into a database here.</li>
      <li>Our host (Cloudflare) keeps routine edge logs for security; we do not mine them.</li>
      <li>Photos of members appear only with consent; removal on request.</li>
      <li>This policy changes only when our practice does — the date at the top says so.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing, deliberately. The pages of this site are static files: your
      browser asks for a page and receives it, and nothing follows you
      afterwards. There are no analytics scripts, no tracking pixels, no
      embedded advertising, and no contact form that would ask you to leave
      personal information behind.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you contact us by WhatsApp, phone or email, what you send us stays
      with the club officers who read it, used only to answer you and to
      organise club life. It is not shared further, and it is never passed to
      any service that would repurpose it.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the site runs</h2>
    <p>
      Kadali is served through Cloudflare's network. As with any site on
      Cloudflare, requests are logged at the edge — IP address, timestamp,
      requested URL and browser user agent — for security and abuse
      prevention. We do not run analytics or advertising on top of these
      logs, and a browsing session here cannot be linked to you as a person
      by us.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      The public site sets no cookies and reads none back. Members who
      publish content for the site use a separate, login-protected admin
      area, which has its own authentication on that service; that login is
      not part of the public site.
    </p>

    <h2>Links that leave this site</h2>
    <p>
      Our WhatsApp, email and map links deliberately take you to other
      services, which operate under their own privacy policies. We choose
      links instead of embedded widgets precisely so their code does not run
      on our pages.
    </p>

    <h2>Photos and content</h2>
    <p>
      Photographs of members and events are published only with consent, and
      any photo can be removed on request — write to
      <a href="mailto:hello@example.org">hello@example.org</a> and we will
      take it down promptly. Text and photographs on this site are © Kadali
      unless noted; ask before republishing. Quotations from the vachanas and
      other folk material belong to everyone, and we claim no ownership over
      the heritage we write about.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We update this page only when what we actually do changes, and we
      change the date at the top when we do. If anything here ever looks
      out of step with how the club behaves, please tell us.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Ask us directly — by email at
      <a href="mailto:hello@example.org">hello@example.org</a> or through the
      <a href="/contact">contact page</a>, which lists our phone and
      WhatsApp numbers. A person reads what arrives.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
